WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.119 --> 00:00:02.284
- If it's the weekend,
especially a pay weekend,

00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:03.819
you know, you can kinda
cut up a little bit,

00:00:03.819 --> 00:00:06.314
and then you go up in there on Monday,

00:00:06.314 --> 00:00:08.569
and it's like, what
the hell just happened?

00:00:08.569 --> 00:00:10.361
(swoop)

00:00:10.361 --> 00:00:12.176
(squeak)

00:00:12.176 --> 00:00:16.504
- I think I waste a lot of
money on luxury grocery items.

00:00:16.504 --> 00:00:18.287
I don't need to spend seven

00:00:18.287 --> 00:00:20.476
dollars on a tiny hunk of cheese.

00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:24.567
- About four hundred
dollars eating out a month.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.506
Because I hate to cook.

00:00:26.506 --> 00:00:27.923
- I'm gonna go out on
a limb here and guess

00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:31.051
that my spending vice is
alcohol and going out.

00:00:31.051 --> 00:00:34.850
I'm gonna estimate, like, one
to two hundred per weekend.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.030
I guess in a month, that would be like

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.298
eight hundred to a thousand per month.

00:00:38.298 --> 00:00:40.268
That's like with, for...oh my god, the

00:00:40.268 --> 00:00:43.620
producer's face is terrified right now.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.949
This is a ballpark estimate.

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:49.298
- And I am sure that I
spend too much on Amazon.

00:00:49.298 --> 00:00:50.996
I'll be like, oh my god, it would be

00:00:50.996 --> 00:00:53.177
so great if I had a yoga mat at home,

00:00:53.177 --> 00:00:55.565
and then I'll buy a yoga
mat, and then I don't use it.

00:00:55.565 --> 00:00:56.921
- So I don't think I'm
going to be surprised,

00:00:56.921 --> 00:01:00.410
but it's probably gonna hit me
in the gut, like a gut check.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.238
(sigh)

00:01:02.238 --> 00:01:03.178
Oh my gosh.

00:01:03.178 --> 00:01:04.527
Seamless.

00:01:04.527 --> 00:01:05.656
Domo taco.

00:01:05.656 --> 00:01:08.201
14.24, and I probably could multiply

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.547
that by a thousand times, because

00:01:09.547 --> 00:01:11.626
that's how much Domo Taco I eat.

00:01:11.626 --> 00:01:12.786
Another Domo Taco.

00:01:12.786 --> 00:01:13.619
Domo Taco.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:14.566
Domo Taco purchase.

00:01:14.566 --> 00:01:17.233
(sped up voice)

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.380
It doesn't even have what I ate,

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:26.210
but clearly it must've been
tasty as hell to be 28.72.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.963
(drumroll)

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:28.813
(buzzer)

00:01:28.813 --> 00:01:31.488
It makes me feel like everything

00:01:31.488 --> 00:01:34.025
that my dad tells me as far as, son,

00:01:34.025 --> 00:01:35.449
you need to budget, you need to

00:01:35.449 --> 00:01:36.859
think about what you're buying,

00:01:36.859 --> 00:01:40.243
you don't need to spend 20
dollars when you go eat out,

00:01:40.243 --> 00:01:41.363
it is ringing in my head right now,

00:01:41.363 --> 00:01:42.488
and it's making me say, Trey,

00:01:42.488 --> 00:01:44.075
you have got to get your shit together.

00:01:44.075 --> 00:01:45.294
- One discovery so far, I go to the

00:01:45.294 --> 00:01:48.377
grocery store twice a day on average.

00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:53.014
I spent 21 dollars and 77
cents at the grocery store.

00:01:53.014 --> 00:01:55.856
I spent 14 dollars and 25
cents at that grocery store.

00:01:55.856 --> 00:01:57.315
Nine dollars and 28
cents at a grocery story.

00:01:57.315 --> 00:01:59.982
(voice sped up)

00:02:03.587 --> 00:02:04.768
(drumroll)

00:02:04.768 --> 00:02:05.867
(boing)

00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:06.700
Oh, shit.

00:02:08.145 --> 00:02:10.253
Oooh, that hurts.

00:02:10.253 --> 00:02:14.256
- Okay, Amazon, 22 bucks,
so 100 dollars at CB2,

00:02:14.256 --> 00:02:16.416
another 22 dollars on Amazon,

00:02:16.416 --> 00:02:19.357
(voice sped up)

00:02:19.357 --> 00:02:20.674
(drumroll)

00:02:20.674 --> 00:02:23.058
(boing)

00:02:23.058 --> 00:02:25.411
(sigh)

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.327
Did I really need to buy
sheets from West Elm?

00:02:28.327 --> 00:02:29.355
I wish I could return
them, but I've already

00:02:29.355 --> 00:02:31.573
slept in them and they feel great.

00:02:31.573 --> 00:02:34.600
- All right, so first we
have on the latest statement,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.100
um, Macri Park for 15 dollars.

00:02:38.672 --> 00:02:40.737
Yep, that's a bar, so that checks out.

00:02:40.737 --> 00:02:44.090
23.60, that is a restaurant in Brooklyn

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:45.917
where I go to get margaritas.

00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:48.195
So, yep, that checks out as well.

00:02:48.195 --> 00:02:51.354
(voice sped up)

00:02:51.354 --> 00:02:52.540
(drumroll)

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.072
(dings)

00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:55.537
Oh my god, just in one month?

00:02:55.537 --> 00:02:57.929
I've had so many dumb expenses, oh my god.

00:02:57.929 --> 00:03:00.111
I should just convince
drunk me to take the subway

00:03:00.111 --> 00:03:01.322
instead of hopping into a cab,

00:03:01.322 --> 00:03:03.055
and that would save me so much money.

00:03:03.055 --> 00:03:03.888
(swoop)

00:03:03.888 --> 00:03:06.539
It is very easy and quick to spend money,

00:03:06.539 --> 00:03:09.689
and it's nothing but a tap,
a tap of that Domo Taco,

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.225
the food's there in 30 minutes.

00:03:11.225 --> 00:03:14.753
But five taps of that Domo
Taco and you have got,

00:03:14.753 --> 00:03:17.024
you know, you're out of maybe 100 dollars.

00:03:17.024 --> 00:03:19.397
- I feel like I thought
that I was saving money,

00:03:19.397 --> 00:03:21.165
because I haven't bought anything big,

00:03:21.165 --> 00:03:22.617
and everything I've been buying is in

00:03:22.617 --> 00:03:25.568
like 12 to 15 dollar increments,

00:03:25.568 --> 00:03:28.800
but now that I'm looking at
it, those have really added up.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.330
- In general, I mean,
I'm just trying to be

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.463
tighter about my money, always,

00:03:32.463 --> 00:03:34.452
and try to think through smarter ways

00:03:34.452 --> 00:03:36.159
to track my spending, and how I

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:38.511
enable myself to spend on stuff.

00:03:38.511 --> 00:03:41.282
I think this is very
illuminating for that.

00:03:41.282 --> 00:03:44.090
- If you are privileged
enough and lucky enough

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.757
to be able to treat yourself and

00:03:46.757 --> 00:03:48.732
take care of yourself and pay attention

00:03:48.732 --> 00:03:53.482
to the things that make you
happy, then I say, go for it.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.434
